{"title":"2006 SMT/Advanced Topics Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Advanced_Topics_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/010bd7599fba154380fc43052ce1f2249756e288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}0 &amp; 1\\\\ 3 &amp;0\\end{matrix}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"98\" height=\"43\" />. Find a vertical vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/545c9da7d623ac319c6d2502f13a057c16d33acd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A^8+A^6+A^4+A^2+I)v=\\left(\\begin{matrix}0\\\\11\\end{matrix}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"271\" height=\"43\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3b32228e9105bf0f3dffd78b0b7310083b693d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times2$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> identity matrix).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Advanced_Topics_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we calculate the first couple powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, we quickly see a pattern:\n</p><p><b>Lemma:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b6ad2fb205e44c608cb48928743165891bbf1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^{2n}=\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}3^n &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp; 3^n\\end{matrix}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"132\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><b>Proof:</b> Clearly this is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/02349576cee613512cdf301a365f06c0760acab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Thus, we proceed with an induction arguement.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c72c4551cab660adb972f088444e452d2aa4a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A^{2(n+1)}=A^{2n}\\cdot A\\cdot A=\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}3^n &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp; 3^n\\end{matrix}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}0 &amp; 1\\\\ 3 &amp; 0\\end{matrix}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}0 &amp; 1\\\\ 3 &amp; 0\\end{matrix}\\right)\\]\" width=\"420\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b81ef9d77d78275c8851d9f0c0afff93944eb70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}0 &amp; 3^n\\\\ 3^{n+1} &amp; 0\\end{matrix}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}0 &amp; 1\\\\ 3 &amp; 0\\end{matrix}\\right)\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae1ea4968fcd887dca9cab53eab9a8396f6ac09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}3^{n+1} &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp; 3^{n+1}\\end{matrix}\\right)\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Thus, our proof is complete. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/627ca013b98b7721f09f93ea9de6e78b34ae11a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^8+A^6+A^4+A^2+I=\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}81 &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp; 81\\end{matrix}\\right)+\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}27 &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp; 27\\end{matrix}\\right)+\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}9 &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp; 9\\end{matrix}\\right)+\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}3 &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp; 3\\end{matrix}\\right)+\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}1 &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp; 1\\end{matrix}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"648\" height=\"43\" /> and this is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd10ace548ae83f714881fedf76592df0b8d5dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}121 &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp; 121\\end{matrix}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"97\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Finally, we want to find a vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6b57b073c4866f666016b36d71e38d078f8271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\,\\begin{matrix}121 &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp; 121\\end{matrix}\\right)v=\\left(\\begin{matrix}0\\\\11\\end{matrix}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"178\" height=\"43\" />. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a309d5202316f59481412f59d783745ca52aac10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v=\\left(\\begin{matrix}a\\\\b\\end{matrix}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"71\" height=\"45\" />, we get the system of equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/f/a6f31eee03f8b3b2f40cfede962716d82989d416.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$121a=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169e41bc3f3925ee33285c44588f9537403239dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$121b=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />. From this, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69cefa6855d2216036df094012f7ad2a7e4e204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/6118051aa04c1f1633a6ebd570ed12caf20b47b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{1}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"37\" />, and so our desired vector is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af45c47670c1526d64742805f54d848c86e3d57f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\left(\\begin{matrix}0\\\\ \\frac{1}{11}\\end{matrix}\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"57\" height=\"56\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Advanced_Topics_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Advanced_Topics_Problems\" title=\"2006 SMT/Advanced Topics Problems\">2006 SMT/Advanced Topics Problems</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017211846\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.026 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 118/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4959/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11178:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017211846 and revision id 47189. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}